          "post_id": "541994",
          "text": "<p data-start=\"226\" data-end=\"256\">Consider the following C code:</p><pre data-start=\"258\" data-end=\"387\" data-rawcode=\"int sum = 0;  for (int i = 0; i &lt; n; i++) {     sum += i;      int k = n;     while (k &gt; 0) {         k = k / 2;     } }\" data-pbcklang=\"c_cpp\" data-pbcktabsize=\"\" data-linenums=\"true\" class=\"prettyprint linenums lang-c_cpp\">int sum = 0;\n\nfor (int i = 0; i &lt; n; i++) {\n    sum += i;\n\n    int k = n;\n    while (k &gt; 0) {\n        k = k / 2;\n    }\n}</pre><p data-start=\"389\" data-end=\"417\">What is the time complexity?</p><ol start=\"1\" style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li data-start=\"419\" data-end=\"478\">$O(n)$<br>&nbsp;</li><li data-start=\"419\" data-end=\"478\">$O(\\log n)$<br>&nbsp;</li><li data-start=\"419\" data-end=\"478\">$O(n \\log n)$<br>&nbsp;</li><li data-start=\"419\" data-end=\"478\">$O(n^2)$</li></ol>",
